<title>USA: GE Capital acquires Czech car leasing co.</title>
<headline>GE Capital acquires Czech car leasing co.</headline>
<dateline>STAMFORD, Conn. 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co's GE Capital Services subsidiary said Thursday that it has acquired IMP Leas, the Czech Republic's largest independent car leasing company.</p>
<p>IMP, said the company, will become part of GE Capital's Auto Financial Services business and will retain its name with no major changes to management anticipated.</p>
<p>Terms of the acquisition were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Established in 1994, IMP Leas provides car leasing services to businesses and individuals and is based in Nove Mesto Nad Metuji, in the Czech Republic.</p>
